{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JhbyGwkgZjb8piTFE9pPaK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N57dZHx8oHadzAJeLFnvqM","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/MetaCoach/docs/user-guide.md","content":"# MetaCoach User Guide\n\nWelcome to MetaCoach, your intelligent Meta Ads coaching platform. This guide will help you get started and make the most of all features.\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n1. [Getting Started](#getting-started)\n2. [Dashboard Overview](#dashboard-overview)\n3. [Account Management](#account-management)\n4. [Performance Analytics](#performance-analytics)\n5. [Coaching Recommendations](#coaching-recommendations)\n6. [Reports & Automation](#reports--automation)\n7. [Alerts & Monitoring](#alerts--monitoring)\n8. [Advanced Features](#advanced-features)\n9. [FAQ](#faq)\n\n## Getting Started\n\n### Account Setup\n\n1. **Sign Up**: Create your MetaCoach account with your email address\n2. **Connect Meta Account**: Authorize access to your Meta Ads Manager account\n   - Click \"Connect Account\" on the dashboard\n   - Follow the OAuth flow to grant permissions\n   - Select which ad accounts to link\n3. **Verify Connection**: Your ad accounts will appear in the account selector\n\n### First Login\n\nOn your first login, MetaCoach will:\n- Sync your campaigns, ad sets, and ads\n- Fetch historical performance data (last 30 days)\n- Generate initial recommendations\n- Set up default alert thresholds\n\n## Dashboard Overview\n\n### Main Dashboard Components\n\n**Header Section**\n- Account selector dropdown\n- Time period filter (7d, 30d, 90d)\n- \"Add Account\" button for connecting additional accounts\n\n**Performance Summary Cards**\n- **Spend**: Total ad spend for the period\n- **Impressions**: Total ad impressions\n- **ROAS**: Return on ad spend (revenue/spend ratio)\n- **CTR**: Click-through rate percentage\n\n**Performance Chart**\n- Visual trend of spend and conversions over time\n- Hover to see daily values\n- Click legend to toggle metrics on/off\n\n**Campaigns Table**\n- List of all campaigns with key metrics\n- Sort by any column\n- Filter by status or objective\n- Click a campaign for detailed view\n\n**Recommendations Panel**\n- Top coaching recommendations for your account\n- Color-coded by priority (Red=High, Yellow=Medium, Blue=Low)\n- Click any recommendation to see detailed explanation\n\n## Account Management\n\n### Connecting Multiple Accounts\n\n1. Click \"Add Account\" button\n2. Complete the Meta OAuth flow\n3. Select accounts to link\n4. All linked accounts appear in the dropdown\n\n### Switching Accounts\n\n1. Click the account dropdown at the top\n2. Select a different account\n3. Dashboard updates automatically with new account's data\n\n### Account Settings\n\n- **Currency**: Automatically set from your Meta account\n- **Time Zone**: Used for report scheduling\n- **Notifications**: Configure alert preferences\n\n## Performance Analytics\n\n### Understanding the Metrics\n\n**ROAS (Return on Ad Spend)**\n- Formula: Revenue ÷ Ad Spend\n- Goal: >2.0x (earn $2+ per $1 spent)\n- Industry averages: 2.0x - 4.0x\n\n**CTR (Click-Through Rate)**\n- Formula: Clicks ÷ Impressions × 100\n- Good: >1.5%\n- Average: 0.8% - 1.5%\n\n**CPC (Cost Per Click)**\n- Formula: Spend ÷ Clicks\n- Lower is better\n- Benchmark: $0.50 - $3.00\n\n**CPA (Cost Per Action)**\n- Formula: Spend ÷ Conversions\n- Depends on industry and product\n- Monitor against your conversion value\n\n### Date Range Selection\n\n- **7 Days**: Short-term trends, rapid optimization\n- **30 Days**: Monthly performance, standard reporting\n- **90 Days**: Quarterly trends, seasonal patterns\n\n### Viewing Campaign Details\n\n1. Click any campaign name in the table\n2. See campaign-specific metrics and trends\n3. View associated ad sets and ads\n4. Access campaign-level recommendations\n\n## Coaching Recommendations\n\n### How Recommendations Work\n\nMetaCoach analyzes your performance data and generates recommendations based on:\n- Historical performance trends\n- Industry benchmarks\n- Campaign structure and setup\n- Audience and creative performance\n\n### Recommendation Types\n\n**Budget Optimization**\n- Increase budget for high-performing campaigns\n- Reallocate from underperformers\n- Optimize daily spend pacing\n\n**Creative Refresh**\n- Replace underperforming creatives\n- Test new formats and messaging\n- Combat audience fatigue\n\n**Audience Expansion**\n- Create lookalike audiences\n- Expand winning audience segments\n- Test new interest/demographic combinations\n\n**Targeting & Setup**\n- Adjust bid strategies\n- Refine audience targeting\n- Improve campaign structure\n\n### Implementing Recommendations\n\n1. Click a recommendation to view details\n2. Read the explanation and data\n3. Review implementation steps\n4. Click \"Implement\" or \"Open in Meta Ads Manager\"\n5. Follow the step-by-step instructions\n6. Return to mark recommendation as completed\n\n### Recommendation Confidence Score\n\n- **90-100%**: High confidence, safe to implement\n- **75-89%**: Medium-high confidence, monitor results\n- **50-74%**: Lower confidence, test first\n- <50%: Informational only, requires validation\n\n## Reports & Automation\n\n### Generating Reports\n\n1. Go to **Reports** section\n2. Click **Generate Report**\n3. Select date range\n4. Choose report type:\n   - Executive Summary (quick overview)\n   - Detailed Analysis (full metrics and charts)\n   - Client Report (branded for sharing)\n5. Click **Generate**\n\n### Report Contents\n\n- Executive summary of key achievements\n- Performance metrics summary\n- Campaign analysis and rankings\n- Trend charts and visualizations\n- Top recommendations\n- Action items for next period\n\n### Exporting Reports\n\n**PDF Download**\n1. Open generated report\n2. Click **Export as PDF**\n3. File downloads to your computer\n\n**Email Delivery**\n1. Click **Send via Email**\n2. Enter recipient email addresses\n3. Choose to attach PDF\n4. Click **Send**\n\n### Report Scheduling\n\n1. Go to **Settings** > **Report Schedule**\n2. Click **Create Schedule**\n3. Select frequency (Daily/Weekly/Monthly)\n4. Choose send time and day\n5. Add recipient email addresses\n6. Click **Enable**\n\n**Schedule Management**\n- View all scheduled reports\n- Edit frequency and recipients\n- Pause/resume schedules\n- Delete schedules\n\n## Alerts & Monitoring\n\n### Understanding Alerts\n\nAlerts notify you of significant changes or issues:\n\n**Critical Alerts**\n- Budget overspend (red)\n- Severe performance drops (>30%)\n- Failed account syncs\n\n**Warning Alerts**\n- Performance decline (20-30%)\n- Approaching budget limits (80%+)\n- Unusual patterns detected\n\n**Info Alerts**\n- Significant performance improvements\n- New optimization opportunities\n\n### Alert Settings\n\n1. Go to **Settings** > **Alerts**\n2. Configure:\n   - Email recipients\n   - Alert sensitivity\n   - Budget alert threshold\n   - Performance thresholds\n\n### Acknowledging Alerts\n\n1. Click notification or visit **Alerts** page\n2. Review alert details\n3. Click **Acknowledge** to mark as read\n4. Recommended action appears below alert\n\n### Email Alerts\n\n- Sent immediately for critical alerts\n- Sent daily digest for warnings\n- Can be customized per alert type\n\n## Advanced Features\n\n### Campaign Cloning\n\nCreate a copy of a successful campaign with modifications:\n\n1. Select a campaign\n2. Click **Clone Campaign**\n3. Enter new name\n4. Optionally modify:\n   - Budget\n   - Start date\n   - Audience (expand by %)\n   - Status (Active/Paused)\n5. Click **Clone**\n6. New campaign created in paused state\n\n### A/B Testing Recommendations\n\nGet suggestions for what to test:\n\n1. Click **A/B Test Recommendations** for a campaign\n2. View suggested tests:\n   - Creative variations\n   - Audience expansion\n   - Bid strategy changes\n3. Click **Create Test** to set up\n4. System creates control and variant\n5. Monitor results after test period\n\n### Competitive Analysis\n\nUnderstand your competitive landscape:\n\n1. Go to **Competitive Insights**\n2. View competitor ad strategies\n3. See creative themes they're using\n4. Check industry benchmarks\n5. Compare your metrics to averages\n\n### Budget Auto-Reallocation\n\nLet AI optimize your budget allocation:\n\n1. Go to **Budget Optimization**\n2. Review suggested reallocations\n3. See expected ROI improvements\n4. Choose approval strategy:\n   - Manual approval for each change\n   - Auto-approve within limits\n5. Monitor reallocation progress\n\n## FAQ\n\n### General Questions\n\n**Q: How often is my data updated?**\nA: Dashboard data refreshes every 15-30 minutes. Reports can be generated on-demand, and scheduled reports run at specified times.\n\n**Q: Can I connect multiple Meta ad accounts?**\nA: Yes, click \"Add Account\" and authorize each account. Switch between them using the dropdown.\n\n**Q: Is my data secure?**\nA: Yes. We use OAuth 2.0 for secure authentication and never store your login credentials.\n\n### Performance & Recommendations\n\n**Q: Why is my ROAS shown as very high?**\nA: ROAS is calculated as revenue/spend. With low spend but high conversions, it can appear inflated. Wait for more data for stability.\n\n**Q: When should I implement a recommendation?**\nA: Implement high-confidence (90%+) recommendations immediately. Test medium-confidence (75-89%) recommendations on a subset of budget first.\n\n**Q: Can I ignore a recommendation?**\nA: Yes, click \"Dismiss\" on any recommendation. It won't appear again unless conditions change.\n\n### Reports & Alerts\n\n**Q: Can I customize my scheduled reports?**\nA: Yes, in Settings > Report Schedule, you can modify format, recipients, frequency, and content.\n\n**Q: How do I disable alerts?**\nA: Go to Settings > Alerts and toggle individual alert types off, or disable all alerts.\n\n**Q: What time zone are reports sent?**\nA: Reports use your account's time zone, set in Settings > Account Settings.\n\n### Troubleshooting\n\n**Q: Data isn't updating**\nA: Try refreshing the page or disconnecting/reconnecting your account.\n\n**Q: Can't see my campaigns**\nA: Ensure you've:\n1. Authorized all necessary permissions\n2. Selected the correct account in dropdown\n3. Account has active campaigns\n\n**Q: Recommendations seem inaccurate**\nA: Recommendations improve with more data. They need at least 7 days of performance history to be reliable.\n\n## Getting Help\n\n- **Live Chat**: Available 9am-9pm EST, Mon-Fri\n- **Email Support**: support@metacoach.example.com\n- **Knowledge Base**: docs.metacoach.example.com\n- **Video Tutorials**: youtube.com/metacoach\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Check Dashboard Daily**: Quick pulse on campaign health\n2. **Review Recommendations Weekly**: Implement high-confidence ones\n3. **Generate Monthly Reports**: Track progress and trends\n4. **Adjust Based on Data**: Let analytics guide decisions\n5. **Test Before Scaling**: Small budget tests reduce risk\n6. **Monitor Alerts**: Catch issues early\n7. **Use Competitive Insights**: Stay ahead of competition\n\n## What's Next?\n\n- [Advanced Campaign Strategies](#)\n- [ROI Optimization Techniques](#)\n- [Industry-Specific Best Practices](#)\n- [API Documentation](#)\n\n---\n\nLast Updated: April 2024\nMetaCoach v1.0\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4427,"cache_read_input_tokens":149643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4427},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a331d24-95f8-4ac4-b133-d876c4186d76","uuid":"7d04da9a-8743-454b-b5f3-16391f82610f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N57dZHx8oHadzAJeLFnvqM","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/MetaCoach/docs/user-guide.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a331d24-95f8-4ac4-b133-d876c4186d76","uuid":"92e9fe86-e623-4a18-80cf-3131c8d8b2aa","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/MetaCoach/docs/user-guide.md","content":"# MetaCoach User Guide\n\nWelcome to MetaCoach, your intelligent Meta Ads coaching platform. This guide will help you get started and make the most of all features.\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n1. [Getting Started](#getting-started)\n2. [Dashboard Overview](#dashboard-overview)\n3. [Account Management](#account-management)\n4. [Performance Analytics](#performance-analytics)\n5. [Coaching Recommendations](#coaching-recommendations)\n6. [Reports & Automation](#reports--automation)\n7. [Alerts & Monitoring](#alerts--monitoring)\n8. [Advanced Features](#advanced-features)\n9. [FAQ](#faq)\n\n## Getting Started\n\n### Account Setup\n\n1. **Sign Up**: Create your MetaCoach account with your email address\n2. **Connect Meta Account**: Authorize access to your Meta Ads Manager account\n   - Click \"Connect Account\" on the dashboard\n   - Follow the OAuth flow to grant permissions\n   - Select which ad accounts to link\n3. **Verify Connection**: Your ad accounts will appear in the account selector\n\n### First Login\n\nOn your first login, MetaCoach will:\n- Sync your campaigns, ad sets, and ads\n- Fetch historical performance data (last 30 days)\n- Generate initial recommendations\n- Set up default alert thresholds\n\n## Dashboard Overview\n\n### Main Dashboard Components\n\n**Header Section**\n- Account selector dropdown\n- Time period filter (7d, 30d, 90d)\n- \"Add Account\" button for connecting additional accounts\n\n**Performance Summary Cards**\n- **Spend**: Total ad spend for the period\n- **Impressions**: Total ad impressions\n- **ROAS**: Return on ad spend (revenue/spend ratio)\n- **CTR**: Click-through rate percentage\n\n**Performance Chart**\n- Visual trend of spend and conversions over time\n- Hover to see daily values\n- Click legend to toggle metrics on/off\n\n**Campaigns Table**\n- List of all campaigns with key metrics\n- Sort by any column\n- Filter by status or objective\n- Click a campaign for detailed view\n\n**Recommendations Panel**\n- Top coaching recommendations for your account\n- Color-coded by priority (Red=High, Yellow=Medium, Blue=Low)\n- Click any recommendation to see detailed explanation\n\n## Account Management\n\n### Connecting Multiple Accounts\n\n1. Click \"Add Account\" button\n2. Complete the Meta OAuth flow\n3. Select accounts to link\n4. All linked accounts appear in the dropdown\n\n### Switching Accounts\n\n1. Click the account dropdown at the top\n2. Select a different account\n3. Dashboard updates automatically with new account's data\n\n### Account Settings\n\n- **Currency**: Automatically set from your Meta account\n- **Time Zone**: Used for report scheduling\n- **Notifications**: Configure alert preferences\n\n## Performance Analytics\n\n### Understanding the Metrics\n\n**ROAS (Return on Ad Spend)**\n- Formula: Revenue ÷ Ad Spend\n- Goal: >2.0x (earn $2+ per $1 spent)\n- Industry averages: 2.0x - 4.0x\n\n**CTR (Click-Through Rate)**\n- Formula: Clicks ÷ Impressions × 100\n- Good: >1.5%\n- Average: 0.8% - 1.5%\n\n**CPC (Cost Per Click)**\n- Formula: Spend ÷ Clicks\n- Lower is better\n- Benchmark: $0.50 - $3.00\n\n**CPA (Cost Per Action)**\n- Formula: Spend ÷ Conversions\n- Depends on industry and product\n- Monitor against your conversion value\n\n### Date Range Selection\n\n- **7 Days**: Short-term trends, rapid optimization\n- **30 Days**: Monthly performance, standard reporting\n- **90 Days**: Quarterly trends, seasonal patterns\n\n### Viewing Campaign Details\n\n1. Click any campaign name in the table\n2. See campaign-specific metrics and trends\n3. View associated ad sets and ads\n4. Access campaign-level recommendations\n\n## Coaching Recommendations\n\n### How Recommendations Work\n\nMetaCoach analyzes your performance data and generates recommendations based on:\n- Historical performance trends\n- Industry benchmarks\n- Campaign structure and setup\n- Audience and creative performance\n\n### Recommendation Types\n\n**Budget Optimization**\n- Increase budget for high-performing campaigns\n- Reallocate from underperformers\n- Optimize daily spend pacing\n\n**Creative Refresh**\n- Replace underperforming creatives\n- Test new formats and messaging\n- Combat audience fatigue\n\n**Audience Expansion**\n- Create lookalike audiences\n- Expand winning audience segments\n- Test new interest/demographic combinations\n\n**Targeting & Setup**\n- Adjust bid strategies\n- Refine audience targeting\n- Improve campaign structure\n\n### Implementing Recommendations\n\n1. Click a recommendation to view details\n2. Read the explanation and data\n3. Review implementation steps\n4. Click \"Implement\" or \"Open in Meta Ads Manager\"\n5. Follow the step-by-step instructions\n6. Return to mark recommendation as completed\n\n### Recommendation Confidence Score\n\n- **90-100%**: High confidence, safe to implement\n- **75-89%**: Medium-high confidence, monitor results\n- **50-74%**: Lower confidence, test first\n- <50%: Informational only, requires validation\n\n## Reports & Automation\n\n### Generating Reports\n\n1. Go to **Reports** section\n2. Click **Generate Report**\n3. Select date range\n4. Choose report type:\n   - Executive Summary (quick overview)\n   - Detailed Analysis (full metrics and charts)\n   - Client Report (branded for sharing)\n5. Click **Generate**\n\n### Report Contents\n\n- Executive summary of key achievements\n- Performance metrics summary\n- Campaign analysis and rankings\n- Trend charts and visualizations\n- Top recommendations\n- Action items for next period\n\n### Exporting Reports\n\n**PDF Download**\n1. Open generated report\n2. Click **Export as PDF**\n3. File downloads to your computer\n\n**Email Delivery**\n1. Click **Send via Email**\n2. Enter recipient email addresses\n3. Choose to attach PDF\n4. Click **Send**\n\n### Report Scheduling\n\n1. Go to **Settings** > **Report Schedule**\n2. Click **Create Schedule**\n3. Select frequency (Daily/Weekly/Monthly)\n4. Choose send time and day\n5. Add recipient email addresses\n6. Click **Enable**\n\n**Schedule Management**\n- View all scheduled reports\n- Edit frequency and recipients\n- Pause/resume schedules\n- Delete schedules\n\n## Alerts & Monitoring\n\n### Understanding Alerts\n\nAlerts notify you of significant changes or issues:\n\n**Critical Alerts**\n- Budget overspend (red)\n- Severe performance drops (>30%)\n- Failed account syncs\n\n**Warning Alerts**\n- Performance decline (20-30%)\n- Approaching budget limits (80%+)\n- Unusual patterns detected\n\n**Info Alerts**\n- Significant performance improvements\n- New optimization opportunities\n\n### Alert Settings\n\n1. Go to **Settings** > **Alerts**\n2. Configure:\n   - Email recipients\n   - Alert sensitivity\n   - Budget alert threshold\n   - Performance thresholds\n\n### Acknowledging Alerts\n\n1. Click notification or visit **Alerts** page\n2. Review alert details\n3. Click **Acknowledge** to mark as read\n4. Recommended action appears below alert\n\n### Email Alerts\n\n- Sent immediately for critical alerts\n- Sent daily digest for warnings\n- Can be customized per alert type\n\n## Advanced Features\n\n### Campaign Cloning\n\nCreate a copy of a successful campaign with modifications:\n\n1. Select a campaign\n2. Click **Clone Campaign**\n3. Enter new name\n4. Optionally modify:\n   - Budget\n   - Start date\n   - Audience (expand by %)\n   - Status (Active/Paused)\n5. Click **Clone**\n6. New campaign created in paused state\n\n### A/B Testing Recommendations\n\nGet suggestions for what to test:\n\n1. Click **A/B Test Recommendations** for a campaign\n2. View suggested tests:\n   - Creative variations\n   - Audience expansion\n   - Bid strategy changes\n3. Click **Create Test** to set up\n4. System creates control and variant\n5. Monitor results after test period\n\n### Competitive Analysis\n\nUnderstand your competitive landscape:\n\n1. Go to **Competitive Insights**\n2. View competitor ad strategies\n3. See creative themes they're using\n4. Check industry benchmarks\n5. Compare your metrics to averages\n\n### Budget Auto-Reallocation\n\nLet AI optimize your budget allocation:\n\n1. Go to **Budget Optimization**\n2. Review suggested reallocations\n3. See expected ROI improvements\n4. Choose approval strategy:\n   - Manual approval for each change\n   - Auto-approve within limits\n5. Monitor reallocation progress\n\n## FAQ\n\n### General Questions\n\n**Q: How often is my data updated?**\nA: Dashboard data refreshes every 15-30 minutes. Reports can be generated on-demand, and scheduled reports run at specified times.\n\n**Q: Can I connect multiple Meta ad accounts?**\nA: Yes, click \"Add Account\" and authorize each account. Switch between them using the dropdown.\n\n**Q: Is my data secure?**\nA: Yes. We use OAuth 2.0 for secure authentication and never store your login credentials.\n\n### Performance & Recommendations\n\n**Q: Why is my ROAS shown as very high?**\nA: ROAS is calculated as revenue/spend. With low spend but high conversions, it can appear inflated. Wait for more data for stability.\n\n**Q: When should I implement a recommendation?**\nA: Implement high-confidence (90%+) recommendations immediately. Test medium-confidence (75-89%) recommendations on a subset of budget first.\n\n**Q: Can I ignore a recommendation?**\nA: Yes, click \"Dismiss\" on any recommendation. It won't appear again unless conditions change.\n\n### Reports & Alerts\n\n**Q: Can I customize my scheduled reports?**\nA: Yes, in Settings > Report Schedule, you can modify format, recipients, frequency, and content.\n\n**Q: How do I disable alerts?**\nA: Go to Settings > Alerts and toggle individual alert types off, or disable all alerts.\n\n**Q: What time zone are reports sent?**\nA: Reports use your account's time zone, set in Settings > Account Settings.\n\n### Troubleshooting\n\n**Q: Data isn't updating**\nA: Try refreshing the page or disconnecting/reconnecting your account.\n\n**Q: Can't see my campaigns**\nA: Ensure you've:\n1. Authorized all necessary permissions\n2. Selected the correct account in dropdown\n3. Account has active campaigns\n\n**Q: Recommendations seem inaccurate**\nA: Recommendations improve with more data. They need at least 7 days of performance history to be reliable.\n\n## Getting Help\n\n- **Live Chat**: Available 9am-9pm EST, Mon-Fri\n- **Email Support**: support@metacoach.example.com\n- **Knowledge Base**: docs.metacoach.example.com\n- **Video Tutorials**: youtube.com/metacoach\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Check Dashboard Daily**: Quick pulse on campaign health\n2. **Review Recommendations Weekly**: Implement high-confidence ones\n3. **Generate Monthly Reports**: Track progress and trends\n4. **Adjust Based on Data**: Let analytics guide decisions\n5. **Test Before Scaling**: Small budget tests reduce risk\n6. **Monitor Alerts**: Catch issues early\n7. **Use Competitive Insights**: Stay ahead of competition\n\n## What's Next?\n\n- [Advanced Campaign Strategies](#)\n- [ROI Optimization Techniques](#)\n- [Industry-Specific Best Practices](#)\n- [API Documentation](#)\n\n---\n\nLast Updated: April 2024\nMetaCoach v1.0\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
