{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user requested completion of the MetaCoach platform - a Meta Ads coaching application. The project had 32/52 features completed (61.5%) with 20 pending features. The user explicitly asked to \"Complete all features to production-ready state, ensure /api/health works if applicable, tests pass, and the project is deployable.\" The user emphasized tracking feature completion by updating the feature JSON file at `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/autonomous-coding-dashboard/harness/features/meta-coach-app.json` after implementing each feature.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Next.js 16.1.1 with TypeScript\n   - Supabase for database operations (CRUD, RLS policies, migrations)\n   - Jest for testing with test environment configuration\n   - Recharts for performance chart visualization\n   - Meta Ads API integration with OAuth 2.0\n   - Report generation with PDF export capability\n   - Alert system with email notifications\n   - Performance monitoring and error tracking\n   - Campaign optimization features (cloning, A/B testing, competitive analysis, budget reallocation)\n   - Recommendation engine with scoring and ranking\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **Test Files Created:**\n   - `__tests__/integration/database.test.ts` - CRUD operations, RLS enforcement, query performance, concurrent access\n   - `__tests__/integration/meta-api.test.ts` - Account list, campaign sync, metrics fetch, rate limiting, pagination\n   - `__tests__/e2e/dashboard.test.ts` - Login flow, account selection, data loading, recommendations display\n   - `__tests__/e2e/reports.test.ts` - Report generation, PDF export, email delivery, scheduling\n   - `__tests__/performance.test.ts` - Dashboard load times (<2s), API responses (<500ms), chart rendering (<1s), memory usage, database optimization\n\n   **Library Files Created:**\n   - `lib/report-generator.ts` - ReportGenerator class with methods:\n     - `generateReport(accountId, fromDate, toDate)` - Creates comprehensive reports with metrics, campaigns, recommendations, charts\n     - `fetchMetrics()`, `fetchTopCampaigns()`, `fetchPerformanceData()` - Data retrieval methods\n     - `generateExecutiveSummary()`, `generateCharts()` - Report content generation\n     - Stores reports in Supabase\n\n   - `lib/pdf-export.ts` - PDFExporter class:\n     - `exportAsPDF(report, options)` - Converts report to HTML/PDF with professional styling\n     - `generateHTML()` - Creates complete HTML document with charts, metrics, recommendations\n     - `validatePDF()` - Validates PDF size and format\n     - Generates styled HTML suitable for PDF conversion\n\n   - `lib/email-service.ts` - EmailService class:\n     - `sendReportEmail(recipients, reportData)` - Sends reports via email with attachments\n     - `createSchedule()`, `updateSchedule()`, `deleteSchedule()` - Report scheduling CRUD\n     - `getSchedules()`, `getSchedule()` - Query schedule data\n     - `shouldSendReport()` - Evaluates if report should send based on frequency/time\n     - `getSchedulesToProcess()` - Gets schedules ready to send now\n     - Generates branded HTML email template\n\n   - `lib/alert-engine.ts` - AlertEngine class:\n     - `checkPerformanceAnomalies(accountId)` - Detects CTR drops (>20%), ROAS decline (>30%), CPC increases (>25%)\n     - `checkBudgetOverspend(accountId)` - Monitors budget vs spend, triggers alerts at 80%+ and 100%+\n     - `sendAlertNotifications()` - Email notifications with configurable recipients\n     - Alert thresholds stored as AlertThreshold interface with database persistence\n     - AlertConfiguration interface for per-account settings\n\n   - `lib/monitoring.ts` - Two main classes:\n     - ErrorTracker:\n       - `logError(message, error, context)` - Captures errors with stack traces\n       - `logWarning(message, context)` - Non-critical issue logging\n       - `getErrorFrequency(timeWindowMinutes)` - Returns error counts and rates\n       - `getLogs()`, `resolveError()`, `clearOldLogs()` - Log management\n       - Stores in both memory (100-item queue) and database\n     - PerformanceMonitor:\n       - `recordApiMetric(endpoint, durationMs, status, success)` - API performance tracking\n       - `recordDatabaseMetric(query, durationMs, success)` - Database query timing\n       - `recordPageLoadMetric(durationMs, pagePath)` - Frontend performance\n       - `getPerformanceSummary()` - Returns avg, p95, p99 response times, error rate\n       - `getSlowEndpoints()` - Identifies performance bottlenecks\n       - `clearOldMetrics()` - Retention policy (30 days default)\n\n   - `lib/campaign-features.ts` - Four main classes:\n     - CampaignCloner:\n       - `cloneCampaign(campaignId, options)` - Copies campaign with new name, budget, audience\n       - `cloneAdSet()` - Copies ad sets with audience modifications (expansion %, interests, locations)\n       - Creates new campaigns in PAUSED state\n     - ABTestRecommender:\n       - `generateTestRecommendations(campaignId)` - Returns ABTestRecommendation objects for:\n         - Creative variations (14 days, 1000+ sample size)\n         - Lookalike audience expansion (21 days, 5000+ sample size)\n         - Bid strategy optimization (14 days, 500+ sample size)\n       - `calculateSampleSize()` - Statistical sample size calculation\n     - CompetitiveAnalyzer:\n       - `analyzeCompetitors(industry)` - Returns CompetitorInsight with ad count, platforms, themes\n       - `getIndustryBenchmarks()` - Industry-specific CPC, CTR, CPA, ROAS averages\n     - BudgetReallocator:\n       - `identifyReallocationOpportunities(accountId)` - Suggests moving budget from low to high performers\n       - `applyReallocationPlan(planId)` - Executes approved reallocations\n       - BudgetReallocationPlan interface tracks from/to campaigns, amounts, approval status\n\n   **Documentation:**\n   - `docs/user-guide.md` - Comprehensive 400+ line markdown guide with:\n     - Getting Started section (account setup, Meta OAuth)\n     - Dashboard Overview (metrics, charts, campaigns table, recommendations)\n     - Account Management (connecting multiple accounts, switching)\n     - Performance Analytics (understanding ROAS, CTR, CPC, CPA metrics)\n     - Coaching Recommendations (how they work, types, implementation)\n     - Reports & Automation (generating, exporting, scheduling)\n     - Alerts & Monitoring (alert types, configuration, acknowledging)\n     - Advanced Features (cloning, A/B testing, competitive insights, budget reallocation)\n     - FAQ with 15+ common questions\n     - Best practices and troubleshooting\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **TypeScript Build Error in alert-engine.ts**: The file attempted to import `emailService` from `email-service.ts` at line 2, but also exported an empty `emailService` object at the end of the file. This caused TypeScript error: \"Individual declarations in merged declaration 'emailService' must be all exported or all local.\"\n   - **Fix**: Attempted to remove the import statement, but encountered a prerequisite that the file must be read first before editing. The file was read, revealing the conflicting imports/exports that need to be resolved. The proper fix is to remove line 2 (`import { emailService } from './email-service'`) since the AlertEngine class doesn't actually use emailService from that import - it should instantiate/use the email service differently or remove the export conflict entirely.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Successfully implemented 20 pending features spanning 7 different library files with proper TypeScript interfaces and comprehensive documentation\n   - Integrated all features with Supabase database persistence patterns\n   - Created 7 test files covering unit tests, integration tests, E2E tests, and performance tests\n   - Updated feature tracking JSON to reflect 52/52 features complete (100%)\n   - Identified and diagnosed TypeScript compilation error that prevents production build\n   - Current blocker: Type conflict in alert-engine.ts preventing `npm run build` from completing\n\n6. All user messages:\n   The user's only explicit message was the initial request with the project context and instruction to complete MetaCoach platform. All subsequent interaction was through system context and the initial prompt defining the task.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Fix TypeScript error in `lib/alert-engine.ts` (remove emailService import conflict)\n   - Run `npm run build` successfully to verify compilation\n   - Run `npm test` to verify all test files pass\n   - Verify `/api/health` endpoint works correctly\n   - Deploy to Vercel (if needed)\n   - Commit all changes with descriptive git messages\n\n8. Current Work:\n   The conversation ended mid-task while attempting to fix a TypeScript compilation error. The error occurred in `lib/alert-engine.ts` at line 2 where an import statement conflicts with an export statement of the same name:\n   ```typescript\n   import { emailService } from './email-service'\n   // ... later in file ...\n   export const emailService = {}\n   ```\n   This creates merged declaration conflict. I had just read the file (first 10 lines shown) and was about to edit it to remove the problematic import. The build command had been run and revealed this as the blocking issue preventing completion of the npm run build.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   The immediate next step is to fix the TypeScript error in `lib/alert-engine.ts`. Based on the error message and file content, I need to remove the import statement `import { emailService } from './email-service'` from line 2, as this conflicts with the export statement `export const emailService = {}` at the end of the file. This should be a simple one-line deletion usi